cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "langquant: a scaffold-as-state research artifact for stateless-LLM continuity via a refreshing language scaffold"
abstract: >-
  langquant is a scaffold-as-state research artifact that tests whether a
  fixed-structure, per-turn-refreshed natural-language scaffold can serve as the
  sole working state for a stateless LLM, with no conversation history in
  the main-model request. The repository provides the executable mechanism,
  typed inspectable state, experiment runners, and exploratory local artifacts.
  Current behavioral scoring and information-flow estimates are documented as
  limitations rather than validated comparative effects.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Bosch Rodriguez"
    given-names: Rolando
    affiliation: Hermes Labs
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-4896-1112"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/hermes-labs-ai/langquant"
keywords:
  - AI reliability
  - LLM reliability
  - scaffold-as-state
  - zero-LLM
  - agent-memory
  - information-theory
  - context-compression
version: "0.1.0"
